![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `n->in_edges()` collection does not guarantee any specific order. Iterating over it and calling `nb.Input` directly can reorder inputs for multi-input operations, leading to silent correctness bugs if other operations are added to this layout pass in the future. Sort the input edges by their destination input slot (`dst_input()`) before adding them to the `NodeBuilder`.

```c
      std::vector<const Edge*> in_edges;
      for (const Edge* in_edge : n->in_edges()) {
        if (!in_edge->IsControlEdge()) {
          in_edges.push_back(in_edge);
        }
      }
      std::sort(in_edges.begin(), in_edges.end(), [](const Edge* a, const Edge* b) {
        return a->dst_input() < b->dst_input();
      });
      for (const Edge* in_edge : in_edges) {
        nb.Input(in_edge->src(), in_edge->src_output());
      }
```

